'' See the source's header. The call through the forward-resulted pointer must carry a
'' RESULT -- 'call.ind i64', not 'call.ind void'.
''
'' EXPECT-NOT is the assertion that matters: the broken compiler emitted
'' 'call.ind void' for the first of the two calls and the value vanished with it. The
'' file has no SUB pointer in it, so a void indirect call can only be this defect.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/procptr-forward-result-typedef.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.ind i64
'' EXPECT-NOT: call.ind void
